#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105904 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105579 :question/id #uuid "c8d31ea4-41c6-5f24-bf7a-a950a30342d7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4253" :question/problem "The area of ​​the triangle $\\triangle ABC$ is $24\\sqrt{2} \\text{ cm}^2.$ Find $AB.$\n\n![](images/e9/e93e732bd04cfda304c2098087548a638d8d869ccf8b1050235e8207825875d3.png)" :question/worked-solution "The formula for the area of the triangle is \n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A}=\\dfrac{1}{2}bc\\sin{A},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\angle{A}$ is between the sides of lengths $b$ and $c.$ \n\nHere\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}c & =AB, \\\\ b & =AC=12\\text{ cm}, \\\\ m∠A & ={45}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince \n\n$$\n\\sin{45^{\\circ}} = \\dfrac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\n$$\n\nwe can calculate $c=AB,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot b\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡A \\\\ 24\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot c\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡{45}^{∘} \\\\ 24\\sqrt{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 12\\cdot c\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}) \\\\ 24\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}} & =3\\cancel{\\sqrt{2}}c \\\\ 24 & =3c \\\\ c & =8\\text{ cm}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that $AB = 8\\,\\textrm{cm}.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "cafdb077-0e02-5e7a-bf78-c3a8aacfb6f7" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050847 :topic/math-academy-id 765 :topic/title "Special Trigonometric Ratios"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186106346 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "82c2824d-4c33-5f10-819c-b4fe7eba4b17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104225} {:answer/id #uuid "982a032b-da28-51db-adfe-d8dc2bae6084" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25}{2}cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104226} {:answer/id #uuid "d9d54c45-2e87-572c-9614-1942d00976fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9cm" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186104227} {:answer/id #uuid "fe