ate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a = ⟨ - 3, 0,-2⟩$, $b = ⟨1, 5,-3⟩$, and $c = ⟨2,-1, 4⟩$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262892 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7f850623-1cf0-5b7f-b020-c07acfebbd8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260983} {:answer/id #uuid "9baefb07-c1d1-5b54-860e-b68104387cb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261224} {:answer/id #uuid "b255695f-5469-5e72-bef9-0b28e1845792" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261451} {:answer/id #uuid "e4a3d805-1618-5717-aa44-a03a5852416b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261886} {:answer/id #uuid "e4d4c9d9-60a8-5e94-b5ef-2dd4a95c4889" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "56" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e4a3d805-1618-5717-aa44-a03a5852416b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "28" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261886} :answer-field/id #uuid "40927668-f3a3-5ce4-80d8-9ec8828fb9da" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262239}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "59779a24-408f-5832-999c-31c9f5625f84" :question/math-academy-id "q-128421" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $p=⟨2,2,3⟩,$ $q=⟨4,2,-1⟩,$ and $r=⟨-5,0,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p\\cdot (q\\times r) & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 0 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 \\\\ -5 & 3\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -5 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =2(2\\cdot 3-0\\cdot (-1))-2(4\\cdot 3-(-5)\\cdot (-1))+3(4\\cdot 0-(-5)\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =12-14+30 \\\\  & =28\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|28|=28.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5cc0cb83-5eb1-5dd9-af9f-ee8ca5368146" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "66" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260669} {:answer/id #uuid "788bb643-f360-5e75-ad92-1f1daf3b6599" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260931} {:answer/id #uuid "c59fb9ed-aa8c-55a3-8bca-ec58a0283bdb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "38" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261618} {:answer/id #uuid "ccb90a7b-e64c-5bcf-9e83-02b231607e75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261678} {:answer/id #uuid "fede5c03-7967-5771-bc19-dd1e5e5a6385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262109}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ccb90a7b-e64c-5bcf-9e83-02b231607e75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261678} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0a92faf-5d71-5f25-92c3-12fac1bc6f1b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262516}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8f9b021c-bf51-5fc5-8b75-b8c974a0fbe9" :question/math-academy-id "q-128433" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨0,-1,4⟩,$ $b=⟨3,9,2⟩,$ and $c=⟨2,7,6⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 9 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}9 & 2 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{aligned}|-(-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}3 & 9 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =0+(3\\cdot 6-2\\cdot 2)+4(3\\cdot 7-2\\cdot 9) \\\\  & =14+12 \\\\  & =26\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|26|=26.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186287822 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "416f2b02-f671-5dac-9033-c92a97bb7433" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285396} {:answer/id #uuid "66d33b0d-7ab1-5eac-8f4e-3d2df7928766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285722} {:answer/id #uuid "e258b1f3-74dd-5a16-b9ea-949bbeba773d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286849} {:answer/id #uuid "e508fab7-8c7c-5655-84d6-97881cdb4aae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "53" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286884} {:answer/id #uuid "e5eaf3c4-9cd2-569f-bb87-a49a632e2001" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "35" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186286893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66d33b0d-7ab1-5eac-8f4e-3d2df7928766" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "41" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186285722} :answer-field/id #uuid "cf368173-4107-5226-9931-f9efe2d03ed0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186287573}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "b2a99499-e25e-5c3a-b8fd-38e4eb5f4e8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-18259" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-3,3,1⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,3⟩$ and $c=⟨0,4,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-3)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3((-1)\\cdot 1-4\\cdot 3)-3(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 3)+(2\\cdot 4-0\\cdot (-1)) \\\\  & =39-6+8 \\\\  & =41\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|41|=41.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295164 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c0db0f54-7a45-5d43-9fcd-054949c78c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c0db0f54-7a45-5d43-9fcd-054949c78c87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293684} :answer-field/id #uuid "91e49acb-95ca-5b40-a0e2-ffd8b5733da3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294456}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fbb0f86b-7cc9-5ea8-b795-4408792fb13b" :question/math-academy-id "q-280670" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $y=⟨0,1,-1⟩$, and $z=⟨2,0,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(1\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 0)-2(0\\cdot 1-(-1)\\cdot 2)+3(0\\cdot 0-1\\cdot 2) \\\\  & =1-4-6 \\\\  & =-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-9|=9.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295165 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "37cae9e7-d969-5e06-929a-5039d5412e37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293165}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "37cae9e7-d969-5e06-929a-5039d5412e37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293165} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6b9ddd1-8994-5843-973e-8858e59c45a9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294633}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "8009ac60-6b35-55bb-b7cb-31b4072308ca" :question/math-academy-id "q-280671" :question/problem "Calculate the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by $x=⟨1,1,2⟩$, $y=⟨-3,2,0⟩$, and $z=⟨4,-2,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -3 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1\\end{aligned}|+2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(2\\cdot 1-0\\cdot (-2))-1((-3)\\cdot 1-0\\cdot 4)+2((-3)\\cdot (-2)-2\\cdot 4) \\\\  & =2+3-4 \\\\  & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|1|=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35b3feda-548d-5212-bb14-ab63c3adb049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293161}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "35b3feda-548d-5212-bb14-ab63c3adb049" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293161} :answer-field/id #uuid "3654f79e-6420-50ab-9f46-330c40c4756d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294116}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "783ca205-66c5-547b-848c-076696d6e4cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-280712" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $a=⟨1,2,3⟩$, $b=⟨0,5,0⟩$, and $c=⟨4,0,6⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 0 & 6\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{aligned}|-2\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}|+3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1(30)-2(0)+3(-20) \\\\  & =30-0-60 \\\\  & =-30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-30|=30.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295167 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6417e993-0593-5472-a921-eba5a037e141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6417e993-0593-5472-a921-eba5a037e141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293345} :answer-field/id #uuid "108e88d1-9385-56ac-be72-c53c0bca9938" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293975}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c8ebdcbf-5834-5ffb-a71e-6b022b6fe2f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-280716" :question/problem "Compute the volume $V$ of the parallelepiped spanned by the vectors $x=⟨3,1,4⟩$, $y=⟨0,2,5⟩$, and $z=⟨6,0,1⟩.$\n\n$V=${{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "The volume of a parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (y\\times z) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|-1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 6 & 1\\end{aligned}|+4\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =3(2\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 0)-(0\\cdot 1-5\\cdot 6)+4(0\\cdot 0-2\\cdot 6) \\\\  & =6+30-48 \\\\  & =-12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So, the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is \n\n$$\nV=|-12|=12.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326819 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c1b7b71-b2b9-52b7-b3b2-a252ff8b3a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "59" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324209} {:answer/id #uuid "2f47aecc-9c32-5fd9-bb33-9b522561ab80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324348} {:answer/id #uuid "4c521838-fa08-5257-af4e-02df87616189" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324598} {:answer/id #uuid "c2857d99-7846-589d-b5e9-648f4a7b08fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "22" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325641} {:answer/id #uuid "d5bb6ee2-1d36-5d99-992a-5cea026f4b75" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325828}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2f47aecc-9c32-5fd9-bb33-9b522561ab80" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "31" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324348} :answer-field/id #uuid "c18648a9-dbca-508f-b015-0d411d90c876" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326571}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "072fa115-fcc0-55b5-8eb6-62f44d05b685" :question/math-academy-id "q-40221" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨-5,3,0⟩$, $b=⟨2,-1,4⟩$ and $c=⟨1,1,1⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}-5 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =(-5)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|-3\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 4 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|+0\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-5((-1)\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 4)-3(2\\cdot 1-1\\cdot 4)+0 \\\\  & =25+6 \\\\  & =31\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|31|=31.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326926 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6f844ee1-c259-5a95-b62b-bbd5374d3b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324887} {:answer/id #uuid "9d4abec8-a143-5cf6-aa13-c8003ec34d9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325306} {:answer/id #uuid "b02ae5f9-07f7-5ad0-ab01-09d9bba0420c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325470} {:answer/id #uuid "e9e59a19-9725-5ca0-9531-7a13df7b3f14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326032} {:answer/id #uuid "ff3d10eb-7d0b-5944-8d90-7dee6bddee49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326214}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6f844ee1-c259-5a95-b62b-bbd5374d3b1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324887} :answer-field/id #uuid "cc134bae-1f69-5a15-863b-dcc9d6d57c23" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326589}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cf69007e-3a95-53fc-ae94-e7b4176da553" :question/math-academy-id "q-42050" :question/problem "Calculate the volume of the parallelepiped spanned by $a=⟨1,-2,1⟩$, $b=⟨2,-4,1⟩$ and $c=⟨0,2,5⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "The volume of the parallelepiped spanned by three vectors is given by the absolute value of their triple product.\n\nFirst, we compute the triple product:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot (b\\times c) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|-(-2)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|+1\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =((-4)\\cdot 5-2\\cdot 1)+2(2\\cdot 5-0\\cdot 1)+(2\\cdot 2-0\\cdot (-4)) \\\\  & =-22+20+4 \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n    \n\nFinally, we take the absolute value. So the volume of the corresponding parallelepiped is\n\n$$\nV=|2|=2.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Volume of a Parallelepiped Spanned by Three Vectors"}]}
